course: dictionary
lesson: 13671
title: Ingest: to take something in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To ingest something means to take it into your body by swallowing it. It is a formal word, so you will meet it in science and on safety labels, where it can mean food, drink, medicine or any other substance.
explain: Ingest can also mean to take in information and really absorb it. «She read the report and ingested every detail.» Here nobody swallowed anything. It means she took the facts in and understood them.
explain: Look at the words around ingest to check its meaning. «Keep cleaning products out of reach so children cannot ingest them.» The words out of reach and so children cannot tell you it is about swallowing something dangerous.
fact: Ingest means to take something into your body by swallowing it.
fact: Ingest can also mean to take in information and understand it.
fact: «Harmful if ingested» is a safety warning: it means the product is dangerous to swallow.
fact: In digestion, ingestion is the first step: food is ingested, then digested and absorbed.
fact: Ingest is a formal word. In everyday speech, you would usually say eat, swallow or take.
exercise: «The label on the bottle says: harmful if ingested.» What does ingested mean here? | Spilled on the floor | Kept in a cupboard | *Swallowed | Shaken
exercise: In science, the first step of digestion is when food is ingested. What does this step mean? | *Food is eaten and taken into the body | Food is thrown away as waste | Food is weighed on scales | Food is cooked in an oven
exercise: «He read the report and ingested every detail.» What does ingested mean here? | Tore up | Ignored | *Took in and understood | Lost
test:  «Keep cleaning products where small children cannot ingest them.» What does ingest mean here? | Ingested | Read | Sniff | Spill | *Swallow
test: Which word is the noun form of ingest? | Ingesting | *Ingestion | Ingests | Ingest
exam: «Do not let your pet ingest chocolate.» Which word could best replace ingest? | Shake | Lick | Sniff | *Eat
